1
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:21,510
Oh!

2
00:00:21,593 --> 00:00:22,777
This is awful!

3
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,448
I wonder if Auntie Stella and
the construction guys are okay.

4
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:33,508
Ah, looks like the guild made
it through without much damage.

5
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:44,715
It's been a while since I've
taken a good look at this.

6
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,240
Oh, that adventurer.

7
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:49,520
You didn't learn one decent skill?

8
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:53,677
You spent a full three-month term
practicing at every training school,

9
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,580
and you didn't pass one? No.

10
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:56,930
Mmm.

11
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:01,700
Kid, I'm sorry. I really am.

12
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:04,646
But I can't let you
register as an adventurer.

13
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:10,857
It was really fun to be reunited with my

14
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:13,764
instructors from back in
my first training days.

15
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:15,340
Brings back memories.

16
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:18,580
The last time I saw them
was like 15 years ago.

17
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:28,596
I'm a light that's bright and bright.

18
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:31,320
I'm not to do the world.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,320
If you're in love with me,
I'm not to do the world.

20
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,257
I'm not to give up with my own way.

21
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:50,080
I'm not to give up with my own way.

22
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,280
What can you find?

23
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,780
What can you find?

24
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:00,500
Thank you.

25
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,764
I want to train as a swordsman!

26
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,137
Train with me?

27
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,160
Are you sure?

28
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:01,697
Do you happen to have a permit
from the Adventurer's Guild?

29
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,898
I just got one from the Guildmaster!

30
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:07,010
Hmm.

31
00:03:07,093 --> 00:03:08,192
The training is intense.

32
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,817
Are you prepared to
finish no matter how hard?

33
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:11,730
Yes!

34
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,110
That's enough!

35
00:03:18,193 --> 00:03:20,179
Tomorrow will be even more intense!

36
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,400
He will be lucky to last three days.

37
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,200
It is day 10 now.

38
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:43,786
At the very least, the kid has a tenacity
that is definitely nothing to scarlet.

39
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:46,210
Next!

40
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:50,430
Next!

41
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:02,020
Do not drop your sword no matter what!

42
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:04,142
The enemy will not wait for you!

43
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,677
Hard to believe his eyes
are still so full of vigor,

44
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:16,584
even after being put
through such a brutal test.

45
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,479
Hmm, the kid might actually
have a promising future.

46
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:23,860
Hey, Instructor!

47
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:27,217
When do you think I'll be able
to start learning a real skill?

48
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,594
That is not something I decide for you.

49
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:34,214
And can you at least show me what kind
of skill I might be able to learn?

50
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,480
How was that, kid?

51
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,480
That was amazing!

52
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,457
Well, I couldn't see most of it.

53
00:04:58,540 --> 00:04:59,893
Yes, that would figure.

54
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:04,157
It is a swift foot technique that
is even difficult for me to follow.

55
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:07,077
A boy like this probably
couldn't see much of anything.

56
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,572
You kept the same rhythm the entire time!

57
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:11,477
You were steady like a clock!

58
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:17,610
Ha-ha!

59
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,000
Ba! Ba! Ba-ba-ba!

60
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,037
Ha! Ha!

61
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,414
Such latent potential.

62
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:27,153
If nurtured properly, he could match me.

63
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,860
Or surpass me.

64
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:31,200
It's strange.

65
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:34,490
Perry!

66
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:39,871
Why has he not been able to
learn a skill aside from Perry?

67
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,717
All he needs is one.

68
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:44,565
Just one skill that could
be considered useful.

69
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:48,400
That's enough, Noor.
Uh-huh. Unfortunately.

70
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:50,437
Wait, just give me a little more time.

71
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,350
Forget it.

72
00:05:51,433 --> 00:05:53,888
Going further would
only be a waste of time.

73
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:58,131
A parry isn't enough for someone
to make it as a swordsman.

74
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:02,981
Swordsmanship is something he simply
doesn't have the aptitude for.

75
00:06:03,380 --> 00:06:06,457
Perhaps it would be wiser if
you were to choose another path.

76
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:07,370
Who knows?

77
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:10,107
Your talent may be found
in another capacity.

78
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:17,477
there must be another path
for this child whoa whoa

79
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:21,497
really you're serious about
taking part in my training

80
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:24,057
camp the swordsman instructor
told me to try something

81
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:27,597
else sig sent you huh i
had heard he was looking

82
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:31,417
after a little kid but uh
he looks small enough to

83
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,897
get blown away by a light
breeze i would have been

84
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:37,617
adventurer no matter what a
warrior's role is to become

85
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:41,440
The shield for their allies
you understand that mm-hmm,

86
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:45,700
okay, then let's do it

87
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:54,960
I'll give the boy credit.

88
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,220
I never thought he'd get this far

89
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:14,820
Well, talk about being tough and gutsy.

90
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:19,493
If he could just acquire a skill, I
could train this kid to be invincible.

91
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:24,140
I'm sorry, Noor.

92
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,580
I can keep going.

93
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,940
I acknowledge your efforts,

94
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:32,964
but what you have acquired is only a slight
improvement of your natural abilities.

95
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:36,928
Force yourself to continue, you
may very well lose your life.

96
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,020
Sorry, but you'll have to move on.

97
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:42,721
He toughed it out more than most.

98
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:45,702
He deserves to be where
his efforts are rewarded.

99
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:47,745
Please allow me to train here.

100
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:50,420
You really want to do this, kid? I do!

101
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,200
Well, if you insist.

102
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:53,810
Okay, here.

103
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,600
Hit that stick hanging over there.

104
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,452
That's kind of far away.

105
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:00,893
Yeah, yeah, just do it.

106
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:03,760
And once he misses, I
can tell him to get lost.

107
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:06,597
I can already tell he's going
to be a huge pain in the...

108
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:08,480
Um, was that one good enough?

109
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:10,340
Okay, do it again.

110
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:12,720
There, good?

111
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,780
No, no, no, no.

112
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,648
I want nothing to do
with this little twerp.

113
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:24,777
Instructor, why am I doing nothing
but throwing rocks at stuff?

114
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:28,077
Because I just know you're going
to be too much trouble, duh.

115
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,336
I want to use a bow.

116
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:40,800
Now, get a good grip on it and
stand in position A good grip, huh?

117
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:42,360
Like this?

118
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,500
I am so sorry.

119
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:47,457
Trouble, trouble, trouble!

120
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:53,860
Are you serious, kid?

121
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:56,297
That was the last of my training bows.

122
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:57,760
Don't break mine.

123
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,656
My bow can handle even the strongest.

124
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,880
Just stick to throwing stones, got it?

125
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,250
Okay

126
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,800
Who taught you to throw like that?

127
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,217
Nobody taught me.

128
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:20,157
This is just how I've always hunted birds!

129
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:23,593
The super colorful ones that
swoop down and grab rabbits.

130
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:26,697
You've got to be kidding me?

131
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:28,340
That's a thunder flash.

132
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:36,397
It's difficult for even the most seasoned
hunter to bring those things down.

133
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:39,598
Of course, I could totally
do it with my eyes closed.

134
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,200
This is dumb.

135
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,619
There's no point in him being here.

136
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,544
Okay, I think I've seen enough.

137
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:50,020
Get out of here. Huh?

138
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:52,097
But I haven't learned anything yet.

139
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:56,533
I must say, you lack the prudence to
handle any sort of delicate weaponry.

140
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:57,677
You're good with rocks.

141
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:58,701
Keep doing that.

142
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:02,860
Like I said, trouble.

143
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:05,040
He doesn't need a bow.

144
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:07,436
That'd be a waste of everyone's time.

145
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,310
Aha.

146
00:10:11,393 --> 00:10:13,377
You must be the kid
I've been hearing about.

147
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:15,980
Sure, why not? Huh? You mean it?

148
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,160
Come with me.

149
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:18,940
We will start right away.

150
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,640
Sense the enemy's presence,

151
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:28,300
and sneak up on them without
making a sound in your step.

152
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:33,280
He's not bad.

153
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,560
Got it!

154
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,520
You will have to do better than that!

155
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:44,861
There are various traps
rigged along the corridor.

156
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:50,011
Avoid setting off any of the traps and
make your way to this treasure chest.

157
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:51,780
Avoid all the traps, huh?

158
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,180
No problem.

159
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,270
Harry!

160
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:09,080
Don't go!

161
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:11,750
Incredible.

162
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:13,817
Although he...

163
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:16,440
he is missing the point of the exercise.

164
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:21,900
You failed to dismantle the traps and
your situational awareness is abysmal.

165
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,199
You have no hope of becoming a spy.

166
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:29,320
That said, this boy has tenacity
that is beyond comparison.

167
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:31,020
A valuable quality.

168
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:34,286
If he ever gives up on
becoming an adventurer,

169
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:38,302
I will extend an invitation to
join the Royal Intelligence Agency.

170
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:43,297
Oh you're quite young to be
applying for this aren't you?

171
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:48,317
I'm pretty sure there's an age
requirement of at least 15 years old.

172
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,517
I already got a permit
from the guild master.

173
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:53,117
I've trained at a bunch
of the other schools too.

174
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:55,397
Didn't work out.

175
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,697
Oh oh

176
00:11:56,780 --> 00:12:03,780
it

177
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:07,250
seems

178
00:12:07,333 --> 00:12:08,163
the reason

179
00:12:08,246 --> 00:12:09,076
you struggle to is because

180
00:12:09,159 --> 00:12:11,717
there's no mono flowing
through you in the first place.

181
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,682
Why does it not flow through me?

182
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:16,291
Well, perhaps you were just born that way.

183
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:17,880
In which case, then,

184
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:22,256
the only hope of changing that is to
go inside the mono-resonance room.

185
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:23,920
Rizzo... what?

186
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,267
I'm happy to give it a shot.

187
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:31,540
Well, all right.

188
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,706
But leave immediately if it starts
feeling too intense for you.

189
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:38,330
What?

190
00:12:38,413 --> 00:12:40,500
A boy hasn't come outside yet? No, sir.

191
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,300
Crap, that is not good!

192
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:46,017
That room drastically amplifies
all of the human senses,

193
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:47,697
and he's been in there for days!

194
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:50,192
They could kill him if we're not careful!

195
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:52,500
I'm here!

196
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,270
What is it?

197
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:55,640
Are you okay?

198
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,765
Does your body feel all right?

199
00:12:58,300 --> 00:12:59,377
Yeah, I feel fine.

200
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,137
Just a little longer, please.

201
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:03,357
I think I'm about to have a breakthrough.

202
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:04,270
What?

203
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:10,720
This is all I've learned to do.

204
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:15,540
To think you've come this far, yet
all you can manage is tiny flame.

205
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:20,605
It's extremely rare to see someone as
incapable of magic as you seem to be, Gnor.

206
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:24,940
Now look, given your lack of mana,

207
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:28,220
it's actually impressive
how far you've come along.

208
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:29,870
What?

209
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,820
Am I seeing this right?

210
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,317
Is he dual casting?

211
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:36,280
It took me 50 years to get to that point,

212
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:39,217
yet he managed it on his
own in just three months.

213
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:40,700
I'm losing my mind.

214
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,078
This won't help me be an adventurer.

215
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:48,560
Indeed it won't.

216
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,471
Turns out this isn't the right
place for you either, is it?

217
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,180
Such a pity.

218
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:56,480
The kid has so much talent.

219
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:59,460
If only his body were
more attuned to magic.

220
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:04,094
He could have been known throughout
the land as an unparalleled magician.

221
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:07,420
First, let me ask you.

222
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:11,257
Did you undergo the rite of blessing
when you were a small child?

223
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:12,237
Rite of blessing?

224
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,150
What's that?

225
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:17,557
At this school, only those who were selected
in advance and underwent the ceremony?

226
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,470
can train.

227
00:14:18,553 --> 00:14:19,420
I'm so sorry.

228
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:20,878
Well, I don't care.

229
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:23,884
I'm not leaving until you
agree to let me train.

230
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:25,310
Hmm.

231
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:26,660
Do as you wish.

232
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:48,933
I'm not leaving until you
agree to let me train with you!

233
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:50,980
Fine by me.

234
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:01,662
He cannot seriously intend
to stay there forever.

235
00:15:01,780 --> 00:15:03,520
I don't know.

236
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:34,937
I will allow you to participate
in the basics of our training.

237
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:35,961
Although please,

238
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:40,455
understand that there is no guarantee
you will actually acquire a skill.

239
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:47,940
That is most certainly Low Heel.

240
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,534
But how on earth is this even possible?

241
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,660
Yes, but um...

242
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:55,037
However, unfortunately for you,

243
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,917
Low Heel won't be
recognized as a serviceable

244
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,357
skill to make you an
accredited adventurer.

245
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,499
Should have known.

246
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:02,610
I can't...

247
00:16:02,693 --> 00:16:04,100
I can't do anything.

248
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,998
Although it only works on scratches,

249
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:10,797
it's still impressive you
can use low-level healing

250
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:14,233
magic without a natural blessing
already bestowed on you.

251
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:19,080
He performed a miracle all on his own,

252
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:23,144
without undergoing the rite or
using a spirit as an intermediary.

253
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,000
Which, in a manner of speaking,

254
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:29,735
means he can wield the power
of miracles without limit.

255
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:35,480
Master Sane, about Noor.

256
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,880
He's disappeared from the capital?

257
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:43,697
I should have stopped him
while I still had the chance.

258
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:45,720
We can just leave him be, right?

259
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:48,717
That kid's strong enough
to hack it all on his own.

260
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,630
No,

261
00:16:49,713 --> 00:16:51,480
if we help in nurturing his gifts,

262
